A||||6||DJRice||The tow truck just delivered my car,,,,,||||1||
Z||000000||DJRice||05-24-2001||09:04 PM||||All I wanted to do was wash the silly thing.  Is that wrong?  It had bugs all over the nose and windshield....I just wanted to clean it.  And the gosh darned thing wouldnt start after I got finished cleaning it.  I washed the back of the car, but <B><I>I DID NOT SPRAY THE ENGINE BAY!!!!!</B></I>  I had to wait 10 minutes before it would start up after I finished washing it.  And it went two blocks.....But I waited because I was <B><I>sure</B></I> it would start back up....and I waited...and I waited...3 hours later and one call to AAA got it the other two blocks back to my apartment.<P>So what do I check?  It seems to me that if the car wash got her, the next decent rain storm is going to strand me somewhere as well.  It turns over, but doesnt jump to life.<P>This is total garbage.  Any ideas?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||05-24-2001||09:25 PM||||Dillon, sounds like it might be the ignition module. There is no rhythm nor reason as to when they go out. Recently I drove home fine and the next morning it wouldn't fire. Swapped modules and that solved the problem! <BR> You are assuming it was the wash, may have had nothing to do with it. Check for fire.<BR>Coy<P>An old saying: Never assume anything. When you assume all you can assume is you are probably wrong.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 05-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||05-24-2001||10:41 PM||||Make sure you're not out of gas.<BR>You never know.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Sootah||05-25-2001||02:03 PM||||That really is odd considering I was my engine all the time. Kinda hard to let it get all greasy again after you see it clean and shiny. Plus in some cases (Like McKayLee's) it will run cooler after being cleaned. All that dirt coated grease acts like insulation.<P>As far as it not starting after washing, I'd doubt it had anything to do with it. I would agree that it may be the ignition module.<P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||14
Z||000004||84Bill||05-25-2001||02:37 PM||||It's black thats why  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Yeah I'm leaning tward ignition module. Haynes manual has excelent diags to determine what it is. get the manual and an Ohm meter||||reg||6
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||05-25-2001||04:55 PM||||if it was from the water i would pull the distributor cap and make sure its not wet inside.<P>  also how old are your plug wires? if they are oily and squishy they will fail when wet or even damp.<P> another thought - is it possible you got water in the gas tank somehow? gas cap wasnt tight when you hosed the car down? maybe all you need is a couple bottles of dry gas ($1 each - worth a shot).<P>  water in your gas will block the fuel filter and do exactly what you are seeing.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||05-26-2001||10:12 AM||||Turns out it was the ignition coil, but I have a new Ignition module as well...Thanks for the suggestions.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
